{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_md_doc", "label": "CLAUDE.md \u2014 repo canon: layout (v3 = HERB eval harness), session entry via state docs, the graphify navigation graph + refresh rule, the hard rules, and the artefact arm built natively in v3/artefact/.", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_repo_layout", "label": "Repo layout: v3/ is the work \u2014 a lean self-contained HERB evaluation harness (three arms artefact/lucene/vector, scored HERB + RAGAS); root canon plus gitignored docs/ state/handoff complete the picture.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_session_entry_state_docs", "label": "Session entry point: work continues across sessions via gitignored state-transfer documents in docs/state/ (dated, newest = entry point), with the current entry doc read first before anything else.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_graphify_nav_graph", "label": "The graphify navigation graph (graphify-out/graph.json) covers v3/ plus the in-repo state/handoff docs and root canon, wired by bridge edges; query it FIRST before grepping.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_refresh_graph_rule", "label": "After changing files run python refresh_graph.py (repo root) \u2014 the ONLY rebuild path; never graphify --update (drops external-doc bridges); a printed worklist means a doc needs model extraction before the change is done.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_design_before_build", "label": "Hard rule design-before-build: no pipeline code until the relevant stage's design is explicitly signed off by the user; present decided-vs-open and get the sign-off.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_no_historical_comments", "label": "Hard rule no historical/defensive comments: code, docs and commits state only the present as if written correctly the first time \u2014 no previously/now/no-longer/NOT-because narration; remove the mistake, write the correct version plainly.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_docs_track_reality", "label": "Hard rule docs-track-reality: when a decision closes, update the design doc and memory in the same pass by removal of dead content (not banners); dated state/handoff docs are frozen.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_critical_review_rule", "label": "Hard rule critical-review: after writing or changing v3/ code, run /critical-review on the changed files before reporting \u2014 it spawns the read-only critical-reviewer and you resolve findings until the code converges; skip only for trivial non-logic edits.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_artefact_built_in_v3", "label": "The artefact arm is rebuilt natively in v3/artefact/: the deterministic stages exist and are tested \u2014 scan.py, probe.py, derive_corpus.py, resolver_prototype.py \u2014 with the HERB mapping key and DESIGN.md/MODEL_CONTRACTS.md alongside; the chunk \u2192 tag \u2192 facet-retrieval graph is the unbuilt part.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_artefact_graph_spine", "label": "Artefact design canon: the graph spine is closed canon Source \u2192 File \u2192 Chunk \u2192 Tag (the only nodes), hard fields are chunk attributes, and the graph is references into untouched raw source, never copies or mirrors of metadata directories.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_artefact_no_numbers", "label": "Artefact design canon: the model emits no numbers ever (tagger and interpreter); the chunk description is dead and tags are per-chunk contextual phrases.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_artefact_herb_eval_baseline", "label": "herb-eval (Neo4j) is the prior artefact build under the superseded design \u2014 a contrast/forensic baseline only, not adopted; the v3 artefact rebuilds from raw natively, and herb is never queried (oracle-contaminated).", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_md_repo_layout", "target": "claude_md_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_md_session_entry_state_docs", "target": "claude_md_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_md_graphify_nav_graph", "target": "claude_md_doc", "relat